{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And I shall lie with my fathers.</b> In the grave, and in what manner? That you shall carry me from Egypt and bury me in their burial. Another interpretation: <b>and I shall lie</b> in the grave in Egypt, <b>and I shall be carried from Egypt</b> — for at first he was buried in Egypt, as is stated in chapter Nazir: one who finds a dead person takes him as he lies and his 'framework.' What is a 'framework'? Rav Yehuda said, as Scripture says: ונשאתני ממצרים — take with me. And how much is the measure of a framework? He takes damp earth and digs in virgin soil three fingers deep." "<b>כדברך.</b> Defective of yod."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:00.256412271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}